From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 04:20:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Qualify the J604 25G83 firmware build

Add the loaded GPU firmware build measured on a J604 (MacBook Pro
14-inch, M4; macOS stub 25G83) to J604_FIRMWARE. The identity report
on that machine logged:

  TEXT 0x60000 DATA 0x13c000 GKTS 0x5c8df ECAP 0x5c9c2
  sha256 3b368ee42dccc626e84967ff408764710a64bff1594f3cfd2c6e4d34d065248b

The GKTS and ECAP records sit at the offsets firmware() zeroes, so the
admission path hashes the same bytes as the report. The normalized
digest is the same as that of the 8-core J713 image already listed for
the J713; the entry is added for the J604 on its own measurement, not
by reusing the J713 one.

With this entry the J604 passes the board gate and goes on to the PMP
vote, the power-domain hold and the hardware identity check.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs
index e7d6a7f07a..ce2cdf66e4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/hw.rs
@@ -75,9 +75,22 @@ pub(crate) mod t8132 {
 
     /// Loaded builds qualified on the J604 (MacBook Pro 14-inch, M4), matched on the J604's
     /// own measured identity ([`crate::g16::identity::report_unqualified`]). They select the
-    /// same 25G83 graph as [`CONFIG`]; no J713 entry stands in for one, because TEXT differs
-    /// per board after iBoot fills it. Until one is listed the J604 is refused at the board gate.
-    pub(crate) const J604_FIRMWARE: &[FirmwareBuild] = &[];
+    /// same 25G83 graph as [`CONFIG`]; no J713 entry stands in for one, because TEXT can differ
+    /// per board after iBoot fills it. A board whose build is not listed is refused at the
+    /// board gate.
+    pub(crate) const J604_FIRMWARE: &[FirmwareBuild] = &[FirmwareBuild {
+        // Measured on a J604 (stub 25G83) with the identity report. Its normalized digest is the
+        // same as that of the 8-core J713 image above; it is listed here on its own measurement.
+        name: "Apple GFX 25G83 (normalized loaded image, J604)",
+        text_size: 0x60000,
+        data_size: 0x13c000,
+        marker: 0x5c8df,
+        text_sha256: [
+            0x3b, 0x36, 0x8e, 0xe4, 0x2d, 0xcc, 0xc6, 0x26, 0xe8, 0x49, 0x67, 0xff, 0x40, 0x87,
+            0x64, 0x71, 0x0a, 0x64, 0xbf, 0xf1, 0x59, 0x4f, 0x3c, 0xfd, 0x2c, 0x6e, 0x4d, 0x34,
+            0xd0, 0x65, 0x24, 0x8b,
+        ],
+    }];
 }
 
 /// User VA range reported as `vm_start..vm_end`: 42 bits with the final two pages excluded.
